{"shortDescription":"The euro hovered around $1.16, near its weakest level in almost two weeks, as higher oil prices and renewed inflation concerns strengthened expectations for higher interest rates in both the euro area and the US. Oil prices rose after the US said it had attacked an Iranian island in the Strait of H…","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":["The euro hovered around $1.16, near its weakest level in almost two weeks, as higher oil prices and renewed inflation concerns strengthened expectations for higher interest rates in both the euro area and the US. Oil prices rose after the US said it had attacked an Iranian island in the Strait of Hormuz, while Tehran said it had retaliated by targeting US assets in the region, adding to geopolitical and inflationary pressures."]},{"type":"p","children":["Markets are pricing the ECB’s deposit rate at around 2.70% by December, implying roughly an 80% probability of a second rate hike following an expected September move, from the current 2.25%."]},{"type":"p","children":["Investors also see euro-area rates approaching 3% by late 2027."]},{"type":"p","children":["Meanwhile, Fed Chair Kevin Warsh struck a hawkish tone on Friday, warning that inflation has not slowed meaningfully and that the Fed still has “work to do” without clearer evidence of easing price pressures."]},{"type":"p","children":["Markets now see roughly a 60% chance of a September Fed rate hike."]}]},"language":"en","tags":[{"title":"Forex","args":[{"id":"category","value":"forex"}]},{"title":"Trading Economics","args":[{"id":"provider","value":"trading-economics"}]}],"id":"te_news:579560:0","title":"Euro Slips Toward Two-Week Low Amid Rate-Hike Bets","published":1788177083,"urgency":2,"link":"https://tradingeconomics.com/euro-area/currency","permission":"preview","relatedSymbols":[{"symbol":"FX:EURUSD","currency-logoid":"country/US","base-currency-logoid":"country/EU","logo":{"style":"pair","logoid":"country/EU","logo